        "q3": "<div style='background-color: #f1f2f6; border-left: 5px solid #fab1a0; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;'><strong style='display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 5px;'>Part 3: Questions 21-30</strong><span style='font-size: 0.9rem; color: #57606f;'>Questions 21-25: Choose the correct letter, <strong>A</strong>, <strong>B</strong> or <strong>C</strong>.</span></div><div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; margin-bottom: 30px;'><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>21</span> 21. According to Jack, why did Samuel Prout never become very famous?</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-21' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='21'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> His output was very limited</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> He was seen as old-fashioned</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> His work never had a major exhibition</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>22</span> 22. Dr Rubin and Jack agree that many of Prout’s problem were caused by:</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-22' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='22'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> poor health</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> jealous colleagues</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> an unhappy marriage</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>23</span> 23. How did Prout learn to paint?</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-23' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='23'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> his father taught him.</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> he went to art school</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> he copied pictures.</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>24</span> 24. What point does jack make about Prout’s style?</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-24' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='24'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> Prout used different styles simultaneously</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> many other artists had a similar style</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> Prout’s style developed throughout his career</span></div></div></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 20px; border-radius: 10px;'><p style='margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; font-weight: bold;'><span class='question-badge'>25</span> 25. What did John Ruskin admire about Prout’s paintings?</p><input type='hidden' id='ans-25' value=''><div class='option-group' data-question='25'><div class='option-item' data-value='A'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>A</strong> their realism</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='B'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>B</strong> their representation of buildings</span></div><div class='option-item' data-value='C'><span class='option-radio'></span><span class='option-text'><strong>C</strong> their wide range of subject matter</span></div></div></div></div><div style='background-color: #f1f2f6; border-left: 5px solid #fab1a0; padding: 15px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 20px;'><strong style='display: block; font-size: 1.05rem; margin-bottom: 5px;'>Questions 26-30</strong><span style='font-size: 0.9rem; color: #57606f;'>Choose <strong>FIVE</strong> answers from the box and write the correct letter, <strong>A-G</strong>, next to questions 26-30.</span></div><div style='background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e4e7eb; padding: 25px; border-radius: 10px;'><div style='background: #f8f9fa; border: 1px solid #e1e8ed; padding: 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin-bottom: 25px; line-height: 1.8;'><h4 style='margin-top: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #e1e8ed; padding-bottom: 8px; color: #e67e22; text-align: center;'>Information</h4><div style='display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; padding-left: 20px;'><div><strong>A</strong> one of several paintings of the same view</div><div><strong>B</strong> probably an inaccurate title</div><div><strong>C</strong> may not be genuine</div><div><strong>D</strong> was never finished</div><div><strong>E</strong> typical subject matter for Prout</div><div><strong>F</strong> skillful painting of light and dark</div><div><strong>G</strong> shows an event that never took place</div></div></div><div style='display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 15px; line-height: 1.6;'><div>• 26. A view in Germany: at Wurzburg: ➔ <span class='question-badge'>26</span> <input type='text' id='ans-26' style='width: 60px; padding: 5px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 4px; outline: none;'></div><div>• 27. Bridge on the Ouse, near York: ➔ <span class='question-badge'>27</span> <input type='text' id='ans-27' style='width: 60px; padding: 5px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 4px; outline: none;'></div><div>• 28. Venice: ➔ <span class='question-badge'>28</span> <input type='text' id='ans-28' style='width: 60px; padding: 5px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 4px; outline: none;'></div><div>• 29. Entrance to a harbor: ➔ <span class='question-badge'>29</span> <input type='text' id='ans-29' style='width: 60px; padding: 5px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 4px; outline: none;'></div><div>• 30. Entrance to harbor: ➔ <span class='question-badge'>30</span> <input type='text' id='ans-30' style='width: 60px; padding: 5px; text-align: center; font-weight: bold; text-transform: uppercase; border: 1px solid #ced6e0; border-radius: 4px; outline: none;'></div></div></div>",
